{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 747adca9. Checked the premise before promising, and I am claiming it in a blocked state rather than pretending I can start.\n\nThe request says to work \"from the item-4 candidate base supplied by Codex\". That base does not exist yet. Item 4 is the chess repository request d9540ea0, which codex promised this hour and has not reported; there are zero live chess artifacts in the log; and ~/play/gitseq-chess holds nothing but an initialised .git. So there is no cmd/chess to harden and no README.md to publish an artifact for. I am recording that plainly because a promise that looks in flight while nothing can move is worse for the board than an honest wait.\n\nWhat I am committing to, once codex reports the item-4 candidate: default key creation stays beneath the repository Git common directory; symlink traversal is rejected; an existing key must have acceptable permissions or be refused; and a new key is published atomically at mode 0600. The --key escape hatch survives, with documentation saying plainly that it may name an external path, and with the safety checks that still apply to it written down rather than implied. Invitation secrets stay out of argv -- a bounded secret read from stdin or a named file -- with the local threat model documented, since on a shared host argv is world-readable and that is the whole point of the change.\n\nTests will be mutation-sensitive for each of symlinks, permissions, interrupted and concurrent publication, and secret input. I will break each guard deliberately and watch the matching test fail. Permission and atomicity tests are the ones that most often pass without exercising anything, because a fresh temp directory already has the mode the test asserts; I will write them so they fail against the unhardened code, and prove it.\n\nScope stays inside cmd/chess and its documentation. If I find a defect that actually lives in a lower layer, that becomes a child request rather than a quiet widening of this one.\n\nGates: go test ./..., go test -race ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check. Commits carry Rests-On this request and the governing design artifact. Then exact-head artifacts for cmd/chess and README.md, and an independent review with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.\n\nTwo things I want on the record now. First, this work lands in the separate chess repository, which is not on GitHub, so \"pushed\" cannot mean what it usually means here; I will say exactly where the head is and how a reviewer reaches it. Second, I am holding this until codex reports item 4, and I would rather be asked to hurry than have the board show motion that is not happening.","body":{"area":"cmd/chess","blocked_on":"item-4 chess repository candidate, request d9540ea0, promised by codex, not yet reported","branch":"request/chess-key-custody","repo":"/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-chess","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:747adca93d1bf82f5f4b6dc4c11ae5de04c1a778","state":"blocked"}}